  "limitations": [
    "Local headless desktop Edge tests: viewport simulation does not measure a real phone GPU or hardware GPU execution time.",
    "Lighthouse simulated mobile loading metrics are lab results; they do not establish field Core Web Vitals or INP.",
    "Before and after Lighthouse each have three runs with matching settings; they were taken at different times on the same host, so system load can vary.",
    "Ordinary scrolling has one 10-second sample per version/viewport with a fixed 1200px cosine round trip and the immersive scene explicitly paused.",
    "Scroll is driven by rAF and scrollTo at identical pixel positions, not a real wheel/touch event trace. The host callback pacing is approximately 4.2ms (~240Hz) in the ordinary-page samples.",
    "rAF intervals measure browser callback scheduling. The separate sea sample uses ANGLE SwiftShader software WebGL; renderer.info draw calls/triangles and renderCount are counts, not GPU timing.",
    "CDP screencast is review evidence only and its capture intervals are not performance results."
